      "mergeID": "616226bd21da0434abc97292",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Writing this feedback up for a friend, but just like the behaviour on live, users on desktop should be able to hold right click to bring up a cursor. On the Live build this brought up a raycast particle bubble, which could be useful especially if one plays with the HUD disabled. The cursor could also change to a different color like green if hovering over an interactable.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1137] [Feedback - Desktop] Holding right click should bring up a cursor",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6160d2948c8e481cae739311",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm aware that the cursor does pop up regardless when hovering over anything you can click on, but it would be nice to have the ability to bring up the cursor whenever you like.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
